{"title":"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3f9bd7ea38f7336f5a64109d4053d775858f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. For every sequence of integers\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a445cb535eb107651baf273db426f2dc0355d6dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = a_0,a_1,a_2,\\dots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a13cc98d65fa2a9ee4854829b89e8177f7895b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_i \\le i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8356d123f1c8a79f94d5a66a0cb1fd5a9e0639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=0,\\dots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, define another sequence\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64d52ff7f2d1fd2dc29ba3fe78e5fc479f36efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(A)= t(a_0), t(a_1), t(a_2), \\dots, t(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb4c905136ccb96b00da961e72dc453464941ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(a_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> to be the number of  terms in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> that precede the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and are different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Show that, starting from any sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as above, fewer than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> applications of the transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> lead to a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c70417652c375503d3067ffff6cab6bb9705552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(B) = B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider some sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b624f22b1c1e3983b29f5e55a6d6d006eeda500d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = c_0, \\ldots, c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> as the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> has been applied some finite number of times.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1.</b>  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c62f44d421c9b8182fe278e88539f716d6bb596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(c_k) = c_k = j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d050bdffb69e5997e155e59484b5c9638001025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} c_j = \\cdots = c_{j+i} = \\cdots = c_k = j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"17\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d469f24c3035b1c0b766243c8cef52861f38edf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le i \\le k-j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />).\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i> Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7ab3acdca74377555f5f39aa8bef33627eb0ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_0, \\ldots, c_{j-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> are all less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, no other terms that precede <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d3bca74ff10ca42a340a58312dabbcbe2ce363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> can be unequal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.  The lemma follows.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2.</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c62f44d421c9b8182fe278e88539f716d6bb596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(c_k) = c_k = j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc26d1e6908efbcdd1e34e3e45e5e8d90c53bcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^2(c_k) = t(c_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63fd07a1bf01c0484fb61d353ba5bfc51b746ce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(x) = f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" />).\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Since only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> terms precede the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07deae076718a4b24e964f05b00e8417ee84821d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^m(c_i) \\le i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.  This means that we will always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aae152812bd05f0d4539c99876ebd9bb062fb47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^m (c_0), \\ldots, t^m (c_{j-1}) &lt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.  This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d1df862d1a06e85a90fc648bd98424fece5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_j = t(c_j) = \\cdots = c_k = t(c_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />, and the lemma follows by iteration.\n</p><p>Thus we may regard a term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> as <i>stable</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad49d6a6590bcff6b1c68be0aa36e5410984eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(c_k) = c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.  We will call a sequence <i>stable</i> if all of its terms are stable.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 3.</b>  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d68bd33dabc33fc16fe6ae61fda6f77c369637cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k =j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> is not stable, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc815f52f3a86a4dc2611b481e64e2ede663277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(c_k) &gt; c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210fa2b352c9970f8776cd87ce8867dc763d4c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_0, \\ldots, c_{j-1} &lt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />, so we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c97f9807fcb8545b41f30cffcfaaa947e172ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(c_k) \\ge c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.  Equality implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is stable.\n</p><p>We will now prove the problem by induction.  For the base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we have either 0,0 or 0,1, both of which are stable.  Now, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/1796b0c7908680e2309bb8e53b672294ab1a146d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_0), \\ldots, t^{n-2}(a_{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" /> are stable.  We must then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc3daf3f7ca8328f821980de730f23ad91fac3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) \\in \\{ n-2, n-1, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"21\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a24286f3c35f9d60a8f1d5e963482823af0cef3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />, then it is already stable.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/85045a44992aaf0b3c0878cbea1508d6091caabe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"19\" />, then either it is already stable or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9690460b08b839cd5a0251097037c2e7cb8b9f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-1}(a_n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" />, which is stable.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b2fe6672fb976aa307abeacf554b3a2824fbc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) = t^{n-2}(a_{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/01748b6821be7561b89d56c2ae3e2521077f7d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" /> must already be stable.  The only possibilities remaining are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64e7f7288b18373ea5fc477ef240200eb5fbcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) = n-2, t^{n-2}(a_{n-1}) = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530eba3cb60d728e6c991ff5ae84d7b8f659e1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_n) = n-2, t^{n-2}(a_{n-1}) &lt; n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"19\" />.  In the first case, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2192d045f37057bd99a9a16120eff91f5e1abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-1}(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, both of which will make it stable.  In the second case, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503a349ec15706da3cc640d227586691a78aedf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-2}(a_{n-2}) = t^{n-2}(a_{n-1}) &lt; n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"19\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9690460b08b839cd5a0251097037c2e7cb8b9f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-1}(a_n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" />, which will make it stable.  Thus the induction is complete.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO\" title=\"2003 USAMO\">2003 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017083606\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 330/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10347/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   23.189      1 -total\n 39.54%    9.169      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 37.07%    8.597      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 22.21%    5.150      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4883:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017083606 and revision id 54775. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}